INT. LUNAR LAUNDROMAT - "AFTERNOON"

Fluorescent tubes. Rows of dryers bolted to the regolith floor. Behind the glass, a grey horizon and a half-Earth.

GWEN HARLAND (40s, mining coverall) sits on a folding chair. She watches her clothes tumble. Her boot taps once. Stops.

RAFI SOLOMON (20s, hauler, sleeve patched with duct tape) feeds coins into a machine. He misses the slot. Tries again.

Gwen watches him.

GWEN
Takes quarters. Not Euros.

RAFI
I know.

GWEN
Then why--

RAFI
Habit.

He pockets the Euros. Finds a quarter in his lint. Slides it in. The machine accepts it with a sigh.

At the folding table, OLD MR. DAVENPORT (70s, cardigan, crossword) fills in a square. He doesn't look up.

MR. DAVENPORT
Seven letters. "Where the sun used to be."

GWEN
Horizon.

MR. DAVENPORT
Eight.

RAFI
Daylight.

MR. DAVENPORT
Seven. Thank you.

He writes it in.

Rafi sits two chairs from Gwen. They both watch the dryers. His reflection and hers shiver in the glass.

GWEN
You new?

RAFI
Second shift.

GWEN
Ah.

A dryer buzzes. She stands. Unloads warm socks into a plastic basket. She hands him one that fell.

He takes it. Folds it into thirds.

RAFI
It's quiet down here.

GWEN
It's the only place it is.

She sits again. This time, she leaves the chair between them empty on purpose. He notices. He doesn't move.

Mr. Davenport turns the crossword over and starts a new one.

Outside, the dust settles. Inside, the machines turn.
